# RDF Unreleased Release Notes

## Unreleased

-- New Features --

[New] rdf_phase_hook_install / rdf_phase_hook_uninstall (state/rdf-bus.sh): activate
      the phase scope guard on rdf/phase-* branches through an includeIf "onbranch:"
      include that chains the project's own hooks; uninstall removes the include,
      .git/rdf-hooks.inc and .git/rdf-hooks/; needs git >= 2.23 (rc 2 below, where
      /r-build keeps the post-merge scope check)

-- Bug Fixes --

[Fix] phase scope guard never engaged outside RDF's own checkout: /r-build copied the
      hook to .git/worktrees/<id>/hooks, which git never reads, and the hook found its
      helpers only through an in-tree state/rdf-bus.sh; it now installs through
      rdf_phase_hook_install and reads ~/.rdf/state (I-2)
[Fix] pre-commit hook takes the session id from the phase branch name (no
      CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID needed: Codex sessions, manual commits) and checks the
      worktree's and the main worktree's session pointers before legacy fallbacks
[Fix] /r-build worktree dispatch payload carries PROJECT_ROOT_MAIN, which dispatcher
      steps (a) and (b) already read
[Fix] phase scope checks C-quoted non-ASCII, '"' and '\' paths, so declared in-scope
      files with such names were rejected: the pre-commit hook and the dispatcher's
      post-merge check list paths with -z (a newline-embedded name is always out of
      scope); the engineer dirty check and pre-commit-validate.sh use
      core.quotePath=false (non-ASCII names only)
[Fix] /r-build parallel-worktree phases ran outside their worktree: the added isolation:
      "worktree" forked each dispatcher from origin's default branch onto worktree-agent-*
      (stale base, commits outside the scope guard); dispatch now starts inside the phase
      worktree, and the dispatcher fails the phase anywhere but an rdf/phase-<N>-* top level
[Fix] /r-build worktree merge failed for every phase after the first: `git rebase <base>
      <branch>` cannot check out a branch held by its worktree (rc 128); it now rebases in
      the worktree, ff-merges from the main worktree, and refuses a phase branch with no
      commits; the controller's cd into a worktree is absolute
[Fix] /r-build worktree cleanup deleted the dispatcher's result files with the worktree's
      ignored .rdf/ (now copied to the main .rdf/work-output first), and the dispatcher's
      plan sync overwrote the committed plan, leaving the worktree dirty so git worktree
      remove refused it (only an untracked legacy plan is copied now)

-- Changes --

[Change] pre-commit anti-pattern classes scan shell files only (.sh/.bash or a sh/bash
         shebang; .bats excluded) and are off outside RDF's own checkout unless enabled
         with "# anti-pattern-enable: <class>|all" in .rdf/governance/ignore.md, where
         opt-outs are now read too
